window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-160e62101398766a"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"skill-controls\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"skill\">Skill 控制</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>Skill 是由指令和配套资源组成的可复用工作流。ChatGPT 工作区 Skill、由 ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 或 IDE 扩展中所涵盖的本地功能使用的文件系统 Skill，以及封装了 Skill 的插件，分别具有不同的生命周期和访问控制。</p> <p>如需了解完整的管理模型，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"distinguish-the-distribution-models\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"skill-distribution-and-administration\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"skill_1\">Skill 的分发与管理</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>分发模式</th> <th>适用场景</th> <th>管理边界</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>ChatGPT 工作区 Skill</td> <td>通过受支持的 ChatGPT 工作区功能共享或安装经过批准的工作流</td> <td>ChatGPT 工作区的 Skill 权限与生命周期控制</td> </tr> <tr> <td>本地文件系统 Skill</td> <td>从代码仓库、用户、管理员或系统内置位置加载已安装的工作流</td> <td>文件系统分发、本地客户端配置与运行时权限</td> </tr> <tr> <td>插件</td> <td>将一个或多个 Skill 与可选的连接器、MCP 服务器、钩子和展示元数据封装在一起</td> <td>插件可用性与安装，以及针对其中每项封装能力分别设置的控制</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>ChatGPT 工作区 Skill 分发、本地文件系统 Skill 安装，以及特定使用界面的插件安装，是彼此独立的路径。移动一个 Skill 并不会转移 ChatGPT 工作区所有权、共享状态、角色分配、插件安装状态或连接器授权。</p> <p>插件可以在 ChatGPT 网页版、桌面版和移动版的 Chat 与 Work 中使用，也可以在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Codex 以及 Codex CLI 的插件浏览器中使用。IDE 扩展不支持插件。这些受支持的使用界面都从 ChatGPT 与 Codex 共用的同一个通用目录中获取公开插件。</p> <p><a id=\"owning-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">各项控制的归属</h2> <p>文件系统位置和编写方法请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">构建 Skill</a>；当前工作区操作流程请参阅 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001066-skills-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 中的 Skill（需联网）</a>；插件封装方法请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建插件</a>。</p> <p>ChatGPT 工作区控制不会安装本地文件系统 Skill 或插件。文件系统分发不会分配 ChatGPT 工作区所有权或角色。安装插件不会授予对连接器、MCP 服务器或所连接服务的访问权限。请通过负责相应能力的控制界面分别配置每项能力。</p> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">Skill 与插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">构建 Skill</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员部署指南</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">插件控制</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"skill-controls\">Skill controls</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Skills are reusable workflows made from instructions and supporting resources. ChatGPT workspace Skills, filesystem skills used by covered local capabilities in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, or IDE extension, and plugins that package skills have separate lifecycle and access controls.</p> <p>For the complete administration model, see <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"distinguish-the-distribution-models\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"skill-distribution-and-administration\">Skill distribution and administration</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Distribution model</th> <th>Use it for</th> <th>Administration boundary</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>ChatGPT workspace Skill</td> <td>Sharing or installing an approved workflow through supported ChatGPT workspace features</td> <td>ChatGPT workspace skill permissions and lifecycle controls</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Local filesystem skill</td> <td>Loading an installed workflow from a repository, user, administrator, or bundled system location</td> <td>Filesystem distribution, local client configuration, and runtime permissions</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Plugin</td> <td>Packaging one or more skills with optional connectors, MCP servers, hooks, and presentation metadata</td> <td>Plugin availability and installation, plus the separate controls for every bundled capability</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>ChatGPT workspace skill distribution, local filesystem skill installation, and surface-specific plugin installation are separate paths. Moving a skill doesn't transfer ChatGPT workspace ownership, sharing, role assignments, plugin installation state, or connector authorization.</p> <p>Plugins work in Chat and Work across ChatGPT on the web, desktop, and mobile, in Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app, and through the Codex CLI plugin browser. They aren't available in the IDE extension. Those supported surfaces draw public plugins from one universal directory shared by ChatGPT and Codex.</p> <h2 id=\"owning-controls\">Owning controls</h2> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Build skills</a> for filesystem locations and authoring, <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001066-skills-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Skills in ChatGPT (online)</a> for current workspace procedures, and <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build plugins</a> for plugin packaging.</p> <p>ChatGPT workspace controls don't install local filesystem skills or plugins. Filesystem distribution doesn't assign ChatGPT workspace ownership or roles. Plugin installation doesn't grant access to a connector, MCP server, or connected service. Configure each capability through the control surface that owns it.</p> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">Skills and plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Build skills</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">Plugin controls</a></li> </ul>"};
